cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use HCRD, please cite the software and accompanying preprint."
title: "Hierarchical Convexity-Run Decomposition: Finite-Sample Chord-Lobe Recovery and Interpretable LC-MS Transfer"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Baturin
    given-names: Saveliy
    affiliation: Independent Researcher
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-08-26
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation and reproducibility archive for a finite nonlinear
  geometric decomposition of discrete signals into nested signed chord
  structures, with finite-sample chord-lobe recovery, continuous lobe-scan
  detection theory, bidirectional cross-study LC-MS mass-feature quality
  validation, and conditional external residual-error triage.
keywords:
  - signal decomposition
  - discrete curvature
  - convexity
  - transient morphology
  - persistence
  - LC-MS
  - chromatographic quality control
  - interpretable signal representation
